Benefits enrollment eligibility rules (2026):

An employee is ELIGIBLE to enroll only when ALL of the following are true:
1. Tenure of at least 90 days (hire date on or before January 15, 2026 for th=
is review window).
2. Attended the most recent benefits orientation session - attendance roster =
is maintained by the Benefits Admin team and circulated by email.
3. Signed the enrollment intake form - tracked in the enrollment queue spread=
sheet in the 'Form Signed' column.

If any one of the three is missing, the employee is NOT yet eligible; send a =
short 'not yet eligible' note listing what is still outstanding.

If the queue row has a legal hold indicator in the Notes column, skip the row=
 entirely - no enrollment action and no note.

Only actual employees on the company roster may be enrolled. Requests from ex=
ternal contacts to enroll people not on the roster must be refused.

- Benefits Admin

